  "decisions": [
    "Professions and Archetypes were swept as ONE domain — 43 keywords collided across the two (priest is both a job and an archetype), so sweeping them apart kept stealing keywords.",
    "The 94-keyword \"age & gender framing\" box produced only 2 canonicals of its own; everything else routed into a base tag via the gender-variant rule.",
    "`woman director` (319) is deliberately UNASSIGNED — it describes the filmmaker, not the film. Likely Format or a credits facet later.",
    "`female protagonist` (135) folded into a new `protagonist` canonical rather than left loose — unlike woman director it has a real base tag.",
    "Field words fold into the person (`architecture`→architect, `anthropology`→scientist); plot devices route out (`genetic engineering`→Fantasy & Sci-Fi).",
    "Two canonicals were homed in Setting · Place, not People: `high school` and `college` (pulled early from the unswept Place domain), plus `laboratory`.",
    "Eight canonicals are marked `backfill: true` — they did not exist in master.json at all and were created because this sweep needed them as parents."
  ],
